### Provide Input Surface to CameraX (Kotlin)

Source: https://developer.android.com/reference/kotlin/androidx/camera/core/SurfaceProcessor

This Kotlin function, onInputSurface, is invoked when CameraX requires an input Surface. It demonstrates how to create a Surface backed by a SurfaceTexture, provide it to CameraX, and set up a listener for incoming frames. The Surface should only be released after the provided callback is invoked.

```kotlin
fun onInputSurface(request: SurfaceRequest): Unit {
    // Create Surface based on the request.
    val surfaceTexture = SurfaceTexture(textureName)
    surfaceTexture.setDefaultBufferSize(request.resolution.width, request.resolution.height)
    val surface = Surface(surfaceTexture)

    // Provide the Surface to CameraX, and cleanup when it's no longer used.
    request.provideSurface(surface, executor) { result ->
        surfaceTexture.setOnFrameAvailableListener(null)
        surfaceTexture.release()
        surface.release()
    }

    // Listen to the incoming frames.
    surfaceTexture.setOnFrameAvailableListener({
        // Process the incoming frames and draw to the output Surface from #onOutputSurface
    }, handler)
}
```

