### API reference > SurfaceProcessor

Source: https://developer.android.com/reference/kotlin/androidx/camera/core/SurfaceProcessor

The `SurfaceProcessor` interface is designed for implementing GPU-based post-processing effects for the `Preview` UseCase in CameraX. Implementations of this interface will handle both the input and output `Surface`s, and it is recommended to utilize graphics APIs like OpenGL or Vulkan for efficient Surface access. If your implementation encounters issues such as resource allocation failures, it should signal this to CameraX by throwing a `ProcessingException` within either `onInputSurface` or `onOutputSurface`. In cases where an error occurs after the processing pipeline has started, the implementation should invalidate the input `Surface` by calling `invalidate` and then throw a `ProcessingException` upon the next invocation of `onInputSurface`. Once a `ProcessingException` is thrown, CameraX will consider the error unrecoverable and halt the pipeline. For `PREVIEW` targets, CameraX will not propagate this error to the application, making it the implementation's responsibility to notify the app.